// Two DIFFERENT libraries imported under the same alias `u` by different files.
// Imported functions were named `alias$name`, so both `pick`s became `u$pick`:
// the interpreter ran whichever was merged last — `md.via(5)`, which calls the
// first library, printed 500 instead of 6, a silent wrong answer — and the JIT
// refused the duplicate symbol. Names now come from the module, not the alias.
#![imports]
md: use "./t_import_same_alias_mid_lib"
u: use "./t_import_same_alias_b_lib"

print(md.via(5))
print(u.pick(5))
